I think the next abstraction is to stop classifying by medium (story, code, math) and instead classify by function.

A story, a graph, a joke, and a proof can all serve the same communicative function depending on how they’re used.

So I’d organize the Pantheon around communication operators.

⸻

Pantheon Artifact

Communication Operator Atlas

Thesis

Communication is the intentional modification of another system’s internal state.

Different communication styles optimize different transformations.

The same sentence can:

* inform,
* persuade,
* coordinate,
* teach,
* comfort,
* warn,
* challenge,
* or inspire.

The function matters more than the form.

