Layering

One message can operate on several layers simultaneously.

For example:

Literal
↓
Technical
↓
Strategic
↓
Narrative
↓
Symbolic

The more shared context two people have, the more layers they can intentionally encode and decode.

That doesn’t necessarily make a message “more real,” but it can make it richer because multiple compatible interpretations reinforce one another rather than conflict.

⸻

The Pantheon Principle

The highest-leverage communicator doesn’t always speak more.

They choose:

* the right function,
* the right representation,
* the right level of abstraction,
* the right audience,
* and the right time.

The communication succeeds when the intended transformation occurs while remaining faithful to the underlying intent and evidence.

